{
  "id": "EDU047",
  "title": "The Interrupted Thought Queue",
  "family": "learning",
  "category": "language/communication",
  "premise": "A meeting group wants every proposal considered, but overlapping speech bubbles bury a quiet unfinished idea. A visible speaking queue and a shared written option let the group return to each contribution.",
  "hook": "Whose idea fell between the speech bubbles?",
  "visible_action": "Speech bubbles collide, then settle into a queue; a text card joins through a parallel written lane.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "A communication process can create more than one way to contribute.",
  "gate": "Do not equate silence with lack of ideas or prescribe one speaking style for everyone.",
